WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:12.840
Argentina is a country famous for three things:
tango, soccer and… economic crises.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.810
Although, the later one, that might change
sooner than expected…

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:21.800
Yes, dear viewer, we are talking again about
LITHIUM, “white gold”, the new oil, and

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:27.250
the stuff that batteries are made of. Lithium
is what powers your smartphone, your laptop

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:32.710
and (maybe) your electric car.

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:37.121
As we said in this other video, Argentina
is, alongside with Chile and Bolivia, one

00:00:37.121 --> 00:00:42.730
of the three countries that make up the so-called
LITHIUM TRIANGLE. The area where between 60

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:46.079
and 80% of the world lithium reserves are
concentrated.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:50.930
From these three countries, Argentina is getting
the biggest attention by international investors.

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:58.670
Yep, you heard that right, the biggest hedge
funds have their eyes on this country. And

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:03.760
this is a big surprise given that Argentina
used to be the bogeyman of finances, the problem

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:09.760
child of economics… and now, well, it’s
growing into a rock star.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:16.440
So today’s question is… What happened
to this country which improved their image

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:21.610
in such a short time? Can they really become
the leader of this lithium race? And most

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:25.830
important of all… Can lithium turn Argentina
into a new Abu Dhabi?

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:30.780
Today, we’re going to answer all of these
questions… but, before we get started, let’s

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:34.130
take a look at the history.

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:35.680
ARGENTINA FIRST

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:40.060
In the last few years, Argentina had become
the bogeyman for hedge funds. Under the presidency

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:44.530
of CRISTINA FERNANDEZ DE KIRCHNER, Argentina’s
government did whatever they could to scare

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:56.840
away any foreign company who might want to
invest in the country.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:00.910
When it comes to the mining and oil industry,
Kirchner made an interesting move. In 2008,

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:05.670
she passed a law against the repatriation
of capital. This means that if an Australian

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:10.921
mining company made a profit by extracting
oil or minerals on Argentinian soil, the government

00:02:10.921 --> 00:02:16.461
wouldn’t allow the company to send that
money back to Australia. Kirchner’s goal

00:02:16.461 --> 00:02:20.630
was to force these foreign companies to keep
the financial benefits of their mining in

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:21.689
the country.

00:02:21.689 --> 00:02:25.989
Nevertheless, as you can imagine, the consequence
of this law was that most of the foreign companies

00:02:25.989 --> 00:02:31.011
simply stopped doing business in the country.
At the end of the day, why would they, if

00:02:31.011 --> 00:02:33.609
it was forbidden to enjoy the profits at home?

00:02:33.609 --> 00:02:38.519
But… well, this was not enough, the real
turning point for Argentina came in the year

00:02:38.519 --> 00:02:47.900
2012.
Repsol, the largest oil company in Spain,

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:53.280
in the year 1998 merged with the Argentine
YPF. For many years, this brand new company

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:59.079
was called REPSOL-YPF. But one day, Cristina
Fernandez de Kirchner, in a very Donald Trump-esq

00:02:59.079 --> 00:03:05.840
fashion, said ‘Argentina first’… Hashtag,
MAKE ARGENTINA GREAT AGAIN?

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:11.921
‘Companies that stay here, even if their
shareholders are foreigners, are Argentinian

00:03:11.921 --> 00:03:12.921
companies’

00:03:12.921 --> 00:03:18.859
And now you might wonder… Well, what happened
next? Of course, Repsol pursued several lawsuits

00:03:18.859 --> 00:03:23.329
with the government of Argentina. But this
was not the worst thing. The biggest problem

00:03:23.329 --> 00:03:31.330
was that after being nationalized, Argentine
YPF reduced their oil production in half.

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:37.840
Argentina oil production extends decline as
rig activity slows

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:42.709
Yes, yes… I know what you are thinking…
What’s the connection between oil production

00:03:42.709 --> 00:03:48.129
and being owned by private companies or the
government? In fact, there are several state-owned

00:03:48.129 --> 00:03:53.400
oil companies that work really well. For example
there is ARAMCO: it is the biggest dinosaur

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:57.140
juice producer and, still, it is owned by
the Saudi Government.

00:03:57.140 --> 00:04:02.290
The problem here is that, both in the oil,
and the mining industry, you need high-end

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:09.680
gear. And each company has different technologies
and patents. In other words, when YPF wanted

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:14.219
to drill their those oil beds of VACA MUERTA
(BAKA MUERTA), they needed to utilize a complicated

00:04:14.219 --> 00:04:19.000
technology called FRACKING. And there are
only a few companies in the world that have

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:21.900
the machines and the skills to do this kind
of work.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:26.860
This is why it is so common that different
oil companies create joint ventures to exploit

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:31.820
an oil bed. When Repsol left Argentina, YPF
lost a technology partner. And this is why

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:35.980
people say that Kirchner fought against those
bloody Spanish neoliberals… and ended up

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:45.260
partnering the American ones.
Chevron, YPF Sign $1.5 Billion Shale-Oil Deal

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:49.640
But… hold on just a second because this
is not the end of the story. The biggest issue

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:54.700
here is what happens when you take over a
company from one day to the other. Well, the

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:58.580
rest of the businessmen are going to be afraid
of you. And… good luck trying to convince

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:00.690
them to invest in your country.

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:07.760
Think about it, let’s Imagine you have an
oil or mining company… Would you really

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:11.560
dare set up a factory and a lot of facilities
in a place where government can just seize

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:16.090
all of it from you, just like that!? I doubt
it. And this, among other factors, is what

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:19.880
explains why Argentina today has such a big
crisis.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:24.430
But, now Argentina has a new president called
MAURICIO MACRI (MAU RITHIO MAKRI) and… well...

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:31.770
the times, they are a’changing.

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:34.270
WHITE GOLD RUSH IN ARGENTINA

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:38.330
In December, 2015, Mauricio Macri took his
place in the Pink House (the Pink House is

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:47.850
the Argentinian White House). He found a country
in the middle of a bankruptcy. Real inflation

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:52.280
was higher than 40%, dollars were sold on
the black market, and there was no company

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:57.250
willing to invest in the country. And all
of this, despite being one of the wealthiest

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:02.410
countries when it comes to natural resources.
This is why, since the very first moment,

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:08.580
Macri has tried to conduct a 180 degree shift
compared to what his predecessor did.

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:12.750
“Argentina's new government scraps mining
taxes”

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:17.500
In other words, Macri knows that lithium is
a peerless opportunity to repair the accounting

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:22.490
books. Of course, no one expects Argentina
to become the new Dubai overnight. But this

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:26.930
white gold is a huge windfall and that money
could cover the financial gaps of Argentina’s

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:34.720
budget without raising taxes or cutting costs.
And this explains laws like this one.

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:40.030
“Argentina signs mining deal to unify regulations,
attract investment”

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:44.740
In other words, from now on, mining multinationals
have an open door to the country. And… unlike

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:48.900
what happened with the Kirchner era, these
foreign companies can do whatever they want

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:53.640
with their profits. This is happening because
Macri has removed the anti-repatriation law.

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:59.710
If this was not enough, this legislation unifies
mining regulations all across the country.

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:04.460
This means the rules are the same no matter
where the lithium bed is. Further, the mining

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:08.230
companies will not have to pay any special
mining tax anymore.

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:17.200
Industry heavyweights&nbsp;Albemarle Corp., Soc.&nbsp;Quimica
y Minera&nbsp;de Chile SA, Eramet SA and&nbsp;Jiangxi

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:22.580
Ganfeng Lithium Co.&nbsp;are among groups looking
at expanding or building new lithium operations

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:25.040
in Argentina

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:32.870
But hold on a second because things are not
quite as great as they look! Of course, lithium

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:38.400
is a great opportunity for Argentina. But,
as you know, having natural resources does

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:43.500
not mean your country is necessary wealthy.
Many Argentinians fear what they would called

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:47.060
“ a new Potosi (pot-o-see).” This means
they fear that the country would become flooded

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:52.840
with foreign companies that take the resources
and leave without bringing any money to Argentina.

00:07:52.840 --> 00:08:02.630
So the question now becomes... What can Argentina
do to avoid such a catastrophe?

00:08:02.630 --> 00:08:09.070
tHE REAL CHANCE OF ARGENTINA

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:14.750
As we said in a previous video, the real business
of lithium is not lithium itself but the added-value

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:23.860
products you can manufacture with it. At the
time when we recorded this video, a metric

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:29.300
ton of lithium had a market price of $9000.
Nevertheless, if we take that raw material

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:34.990
and turn it into mobile phone batteries, we
could get an income of between $1.5 and $5

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:41.749
million. Of course, this is a very rough estimation,
but it does help us understand something important.

00:08:41.749 --> 00:08:45.749
But… hold on a moment because this is not
as simple as it looks!

00:08:45.749 --> 00:08:51.410
Most of the lithium battery factories are
in countries like the US, Germany or, of course,

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:56.890
China. These three countries have a world-class
network of small companies that provide things

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:58.839
to the big manufacturing plants.

00:08:58.839 --> 00:09:04.920
We are talking about logistics, semiconductors,
and so on. All of these things make the manufacturing

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:09.410
process cheaper and more efficient. But not
only that, this network effect is what attracts

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:13.560
the best engineers and skilled professionals
to these countries. This is the essential

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:16.940
if you want to create a high tech industry
in a country.

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:22.920
I mean, look, good luck trying to convince
a woman who lives in San Francisco and makes

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:28.980
a 6 figure salary to move to Rosario, Argentina,
and work in a factory. As you can imagine,

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:33.610
it’s pretty much impossible.

00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:38.070
So now you might be wondering… What can
Macri do to industrialize his country?

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:42.120
Well, the first thing we have to keep in mind
is this: Silicon Valley was not created in

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:46.579
a day. Nevertheless, Argentina has a great
advantage over California… They can make

00:09:46.579 --> 00:09:49.019
easy money by selling raw lithium.

00:09:49.019 --> 00:09:52.939
Of course, this money can be used by the government
to boost their earnings, but it is also a

00:09:52.939 --> 00:09:57.210
good opportunity to invest in universities
that will train those workers that might can

00:09:57.210 --> 00:10:02.720
start those small companies you need in order
to get the big factories up and running.

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:07.839
Further, the Government can even co-finance
brand new businesses. This is actually the

00:10:07.839 --> 00:10:13.240
formula that helped Israel become a technologic
capital. And so far, it seems that Macri is

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:37.920
committed to working this way.
But… wait a minute because there are some

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:43.811
dark clouds on the horizon. All these opportunities
Argentina has will disappear if Macri, or

00:10:43.811 --> 00:10:48.779
whoever follows him, falls into the temptation
of destroying rule of law, and going back

00:10:48.779 --> 00:10:54.850
to ultra-nationalism which would scare away
foreigners. And… it seems that Cristina

00:10:54.850 --> 00:11:03.999
Fernandez de Kirchner wants to run for office
again…

00:11:03.999 --> 00:11:14.360
So now it is your turn. Do you think Argentina
could restore the rule of law and become a

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:19.129
wealthy country thanks to lithium? Or are
we going to see a new nationalist backlash

00:11:19.129 --> 00:11:24.269
and a new economic crisis? You can leave your
answer in the comment section below.

